# https://github.com/sbt/zinc/issues/226
# The mirror of companion-shadowing: a class added next to an existing object turns the
# term-only name B into a type, which makes the type reference in A.scala ambiguous.
> compile

# add class B next to object q.B
$ copy-file changes/Q.scala Q.scala

# type B in A.scala is now ambiguous between p.B and q.B; A must be recompiled and fail
-> compile
